The collection sugar is carried neutrally: the bracket is the node, and no host head enters the corpus

`[T]`, `{T}` and `{K, V}` parse to `{"[]": [T]}` and `{"{}": [...]}` rather than to Seq, Set and Map
applications, and the `[]` and `{}` value defaults to `{"[]": []}` and `{"{}": []}` rather than a
`Seq.empty` path. The drake surface never named those hosts' types; the parser's 2026-09-16 encoding
did, and Dev's reading of Dictionary's `{K, V1}` slot corrected it. The Scala target alone spells
`Seq[T]`, `Set[T]`, `Map[K, V]` and `Seq.empty`, in one function each, and the renderer contract gains
a `collection` slot so the three expression renderers agree. Twenty definitions re-encode; no
drake file moves. The remaining host names in the carrier — the leaves, and the heads with no drake
form yet, Option first — each need a target-neutral representation of their own.

